":0,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 56.4%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 1.10"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":24.59,"default_fair_val":24.59,"premium_pct":-55.3,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":77.9,"pe_forward":68.6,"pb_trailing":1.2,"pb_forward":1.1,"div_yield":9.92,"ps_ratio":3.1,"fcf_to_ev":6.32,"fcf_to_mcap":8.09,"liab_to_assets":56.4,"cash_to_assets":5.7,"current_ratio":1.1,"roe":1.6,"roa":0.7,"moat":{"ticker":"VALE","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"巴西淡水河谷（VALE）作為全球領先的鐵礦石和鎳生產商，其產品本質上是高度同質化的商品。公司缺乏顯著的品牌溢價能力，客戶購買決策主要基於價格、產品質量標準和供應穩定性，而非品牌忠誠度。在鐵礦石市場，儘管 VALE 是主要供應商，但其定價權受全球供需關係、宏觀經濟週期以及主要競爭對手（如力拓、必和必拓）的產量影響巨大。因此，在品牌定價權方面，VALE 的護城河極為薄弱，難以形成獨立於市場週期的定價優勢。","comment_en":"Vale S.A. (VALE), as a leading global producer of iron ore and nickel, deals in highly commoditized products. The company lacks significant brand premium power; customer purchasing decisions are primarily based on price, quality standards, and supply stability, rather than brand loyalty. In the iron ore market, although VALE is a major supplier, its pricing power is heavily influenced by global supply-demand dynamics, macroeconomic cycles, and the output of major competitors like Rio Tinto and BHP. Consequently, Vale's moat in terms of brand pricing power is extremely weak, making it difficult to form a pricing advantage independent of market cycles."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"VALE 的核心業務是礦產開採，這是一個資本密集且受自然資源稟賦高度影響的行業。雖然公司可能擁有某些開採技術或加工方法的專利，但這些專利通常難以構成持久的、排他性的競爭壁壘。礦產資源的開採權和環境許可證是其運營的關鍵，但這些權利更多是基於政府監管和資源分配，而非技術創新帶來的獨特性。與科技或製藥公司不同，VALE 的業務模式不依賴於專利保護來維持其市場地位，因此在專利和監管壁壘方面得分很低。","comment_en":"VALE's core business is mining, an industry that is capital-intensive and highly dependent on natural resource endowments. While the company may hold patents for certain extraction technologies or processing methods, these patents generally struggle to form lasting, exclusive competitive barriers. Mining rights and environmental permits are critical for its operations, but these are more based on government regulation and resource allocation rather than uniqueness derived from technological innovation. Unlike tech or pharma companies, VALE's business model does not rely on patent protection to maintain its market position, thus scoring very low on patents and regulatory barriers."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"對於 VALE 的主要客戶，如鋼鐵製造商，轉換供應商的成本相對較低。雖然更換供應商可能涉及一些行政和物流上的調整，但由於鐵礦石等原材料的標準化程度高，客戶可以相對容易地從其他大型礦業公司採購。然而，對於某些特定規格的鐵礦石或鎳產品，如果 VALE 是少數能穩定供應的生產商，客戶可能面臨一定的轉換難度。但總體而言，這種轉換成本不足以形成強大的客戶黏性，因此得分中等偏低。","comment_en":"For VALE's main customers, such as steel manufacturers, the cost of switching suppliers is relatively low. While changing suppliers might involve some administrative and logistical adjustments, the high standardization of raw materials like iron ore allows customers to procure from other major mining companies with relative ease. However, for certain specific grades of iron ore or nickel products, if VALE is one of the few producers capable of stable supply, customers might face some difficulty in switching. Overall, these switching costs are not sufficient to create strong customer stickiness, hence the moderately low score."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"網絡效應是指產品或服務的價值隨著用戶數量的增加而增加的現象。VALE 的業務模式是原材料的生產和銷售，這是一個典型的 B2B（企業對企業）的交易，其價值鏈中幾乎不存在網絡效應。客戶購買鐵礦石或鎳，其決策主要基於產品規格、價格和供應可靠性，而非供應商的用戶基礎。因此，VALE 的業務無法從網絡效應中獲益，這方面的護城河幾乎為零。","comment_en":"Network effects refer to the phenomenon where the value of a product or service increases with the number of users. VALE's business model involves the production and sale of raw materials, a typical B2B (business-to-business) transaction where network effects are virtually non-existent in its value chain. Customers purchase iron ore or nickel based primarily on product specifications, price, and supply reliability, not on the supplier's user base. Therefore, VALE's business cannot benefit from network effects, and its moat in this aspect is close to zero."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"VALE 作為全球最大的鐵礦石生產商之一，其規模經濟效應非常顯著。龐大的礦山、先進的開採設備以及優化的物流網絡，使得其單位生產成本遠低於大多數小型競爭對手。這種規模優勢不僅體現在生產環節，也包括採購、研發和融資方面。在鐵礦石行業，規模是建立成本領先地位的關鍵因素，這為 VALE 提供了一個堅實的護城河，使其能夠在市場價格波動時保持較強的盈利能力，並對新進入者構成顯著障礙。","comment_en":"As one of the world's largest iron ore producers, VALE benefits from significant economies of scale. Its vast mines, advanced extraction equipment, and optimized logistics network result in unit production costs far lower than those of most smaller competitors. This scale advantage is evident not only in production but also in procurement, R&D, and financing. In the iron ore industry, scale is a critical factor in establishing a cost leadership position, providing VALE with a solid moat that allows it to maintain strong profitability during market price fluctuations and poses a significant barrier to new entrants."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"VALE 擁有巴西豐富且高品質的鐵礦石儲量，特別是其位於巴西東南部礦帶的礦山，這些礦產資源的地理位置和礦石品位具有獨特性。這些優質礦產資源的獲取和開發需要巨額的資本投入和漫長的時間，形成了事實上的進入壁壘。雖然其他礦業巨頭也在全球範圍內擁有礦產，但 VALE 在巴西的特定礦區資源禀賦和開採條件具有一定的獨特性，這構成了其護城河的一部分，使其能夠在長期內保持競爭優勢。","comment_en":"VALE possesses rich and high-quality iron ore reserves in Brazil, particularly its mines in the southeastern mining belt. The geographical location and ore grade of these mineral resources are unique. Acquiring and developing these high-quality mineral resources requires substantial capital investment and a long time, forming a de facto entry barrier. While other mining giants also own mineral assets globally, VALE's specific resource endowments and mining conditions in its Brazilian concessions offer a degree of uniqueness, forming part of its moat and enabling it to maintain a competitive advantage over the long term."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"VALE 在礦產開採、加工和運輸方面展現出較高的營運效率。公司持續投資於技術升級和流程優化，以降低生產成本、提高產品質量並確保供應穩定性。例如，其在巴西的礦山採用了先進的技術來提高礦石回收率和減少環境影響。儘管礦業營運本身存在固有的週期性和風險，但 VALE 相較於行業平均水平，其營運效率和成本控制能力較為突出，這構成了一定的競爭優勢，有助於其在市場競爭中保持領先地位。","comment_en":"VALE demonstrates high operational efficiency in mining, processing, and transportation. The company continuously invests in technological upgrades and process optimization to reduce production costs, improve product quality, and ensure supply stability. For instance, its mines in Brazil employ advanced technologies to enhance ore recovery rates and minimize environmental impact. Although mining operations inherently involve cyclicality and risks, VALE's operational efficiency and cost control capabilities are more prominent than the industry average, constituting a competitive advantage that helps it maintain a leading position in the market."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"VALE 的資本配置策略在過去經歷了波動。公司在擴張和併購方面曾有過激進的投資，但也面臨過嚴重的安全事故（如 2015 年和 2019 年的巴西礦難）導致的巨額賠償和聲譽損失，這影響了其資本配置的有效性。近年來，公司似乎更注重於優化現有資產、削減債務和恢復股東回報。然而，相較於巴菲特所欣賞的、始終如一且極具洞察力的資本配置者，VALE 的歷史記錄顯示其在資本配置決策上存在一定的風險和不確定性，得分為中等。","comment_en":"VALE's capital allocation strategy has experienced fluctuations in the past. The company has made aggressive investments in expansion and acquisitions, but has also faced substantial compensation and reputational damage due to severe safety incidents (such as the dam collapses in Brazil in 2015 and 2019), impacting the effectiveness of its capital allocation. In recent years, the company appears to be focusing more on optimizing existing assets, reducing debt, and restoring shareholder returns. However, compared to the consistent and insightful capital allocators admired by Buffett, VALE's historical record indicates certain risks and uncertainties in its capital allocation decisions, resulting in a moderate score."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"VALE 的客戶主要是大型鋼鐵企業和其他工業製造商，這些客戶對供應商的依賴度相對較低，因為鐵礦石等大宗商品市場供應商較多，且產品標準化程度高。雖然 VALE 作為主要供應商，能提供穩定的產量和質量，這有助於維持一定的客戶關係，但客戶尋求最佳採購條件的動機始終存在。因此，客戶黏性並非 VALE 的核心競爭力，轉換成本不高意味著客戶保留並非易事，得分中等偏低。","comment_en":"VALE's customers are primarily large steel companies and other industrial manufacturers who have relatively low dependence on any single supplier, given the numerous suppliers in the commodity market for products like iron ore and the high degree of product standardization. While VALE, as a major supplier, can offer stable output and quality, which helps maintain certain customer relationships, the customers' motivation to seek the best procurement terms always exists. Therefore, customer stickiness is not VALE's core competency, and low switching costs imply that customer retention is not easy, resulting in a moderately low score."},"m10_durability":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"VALE 的業務模式（鐵礦石和鎳的開採與銷售）本質上是週期性的，受全球宏觀經濟、基礎設施建設和工業生產的影響極大。雖然鐵礦石作為鋼鐵生產的關鍵原材料，其長期需求相對穩定，但價格波動劇烈。此外，礦業面臨環境、社會和治理（ESG）方面的壓力日益增大，以及潛在的資源枯竭風險。因此，VALE 的業務護城河的持久性受到這些週期性、監管和資源限制的挑戰，得分為中等。","comment_en":"VALE's business model (mining and selling iron ore and nickel) is inherently cyclical, heavily influenced by the global macroeconomy, infrastructure construction, and industrial production. Although iron ore, as a key raw material for steel production, has relatively stable long-term demand, its price fluctuates dramatically. Furthermore, the mining industry faces increasing pressure from environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors, as well as the potential risk of resource depletion. Consequently, the durability of VALE's business moat is challenged by these cyclical factors, regulatory pressures, and resource limitations, leading to a moderate score."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"巴西淡水河谷（VALE）的經濟護城河整體偏弱，主要依賴於其在鐵礦石和鎳行業的規模優勢（M5）和部分獨特的地理資產（M6）。這使其能夠在成本上領先，並在特定區域擁有資源稟賦。然而，其產品的高度商品化嚴重削弱了品牌定價權（M1）、網絡效應（M4）和客戶保留（M9）。專利與監管壁壘（M2）在礦業中作用有限，轉換成本（M3）不高。營運效率（M7）尚可，但資本配置（M8）歷史記錄有待觀察。業務的週期性（M10）也限制了其護城河的持久性。總體而言，VALE 屬於典型的「商品型」公司，其價值主要由市場週期和成本競爭力驅動，而非強大的、可持續的特許經營權或收費橋模式。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Vale S.A. (VALE)'s economic moat is generally weak, primarily relying on its scale advantage (M5) and certain unique geographical assets (M6) in the iron ore and nickel industries. This allows it to lead in costs and possess resource endowments in specific regions. However, the high commoditization of its products significantly weakens its brand pricing power (M1), network effects (M4), and customer retention (M9). Patent and regulatory barriers (M2) play a limited role in mining, and switching costs (M3) are not high. Operational efficiency (M7) is adequate, but its capital allocation (M8) track record is mixed. The cyclical nature of its business (M10) also limits the durability of its moat. Overall, VALE is a typical 'commodity-type' company whose value is driven mainly by market cycles and cost competitiveness, rather than strong, sustainable franchise or toll-bridge-like models.","evidenceHash":"ab3b8a2d1abf6cb80d42c496ce799408db2667c00f57fa5349891c32c0aec5ef","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"staleEvidence","evidenceHash":"ab3b8a2d1abf6cb80d42c496ce799408db2667c00f57fa5349891c32c0aec5ef","currentEvidenceHash":"a8fe827736050171d5b4c31a9e33af8a05d11750b588364831c18aeff0766d9d"},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-06T12:33:07.001Z","evidenceHash":"3cb753d1f8c777bf8825ac7a9c736ebbec2a4874c33379a2a9f393c9485854b6"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-06T12:33:07.001Z","evidenceHash":"3cb753d1f8c777bf8825ac7a9c736ebbec2a4874c33379a2a9f393c9485854b6"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/VALE.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/VALE.png","website":"https://www.vale.com","ceo":"Gustavo Duarte Pimenta","full_time_employees":"65805","description":"Operating globally and within Brazil, Vale S.A. is a major producer and seller of essential raw materials, including iron ore, iron ore pellets, nickel, and copper. Its operations are organized into two primary segments. The Iron Solutions segment is dedicated to the extraction and production of iron ore, pellets, and various other ferrous products, also providing crucial logistics services. Meanwhile, the Energy Transition Materials segment specializes in mining nickel, along with its valuable by-products such as gold, silver, cobalt, and other precious metals. This segment also handles copper, primarily used in construction for piping and electrical cables. Established in 1942, the company was formerly known as Companhia Vale do Rio Doce before officially rebranding as Vale S.A. in May 2009. Vale S.A. is headquartered in Rio De Janeiro, Brazil.","description_en":"Operating globally and within Brazil, Vale S.A. is a major producer and seller of essential raw materials, including iron ore, iron ore pellets, nickel, and copper. Its operations are organized into two primary segments. The Iron Solutions segment is dedicated to the extraction and production of iron ore, pellets, and various other ferrous products, also providing crucial logistics services. Meanwhile, the Energy Transition Materials segment specializes in mining nickel, along with its valuable by-products such as gold, silver, cobalt, and other precious metals. This segment also handles copper, primarily used in construction for piping and electrical cables. Established in 1942, the company was formerly known as Companhia Vale do Rio Doce before officially rebranding as Vale S.A. in May 2009. Vale S.A. is headquartered in Rio De Janeiro, Brazil.","description_zh":"Vale S.A.（美股代碼：VALE）為 Basic Materials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Industrial Materials 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"Praia de Botafogo 186","city":"Rio De Janeiro","state":"RJ","zip":"22250-145","country":"BR","phone":"55 21 3485 5000","full_address":"Praia de Botafogo 186, Rio De Janeiro, RJ 22250-145, BR","range_52w":"10.96-17.94","year_high":17.94,"year_low":10.96,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":10.96,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-30","name":"de Souza Funo Elaine Maria","title":"officer: Accounting Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":7,"price":11.74,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-30","name":"de Souza Funo Elaine Maria","title":"officer: Accounting Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":240,"price":12.55,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-10","name":"Viana Madeira Andre","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":4,"price":14.99,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-10","name":"Viana Madeira Andre","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":5,"price":14.63,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-10","name":"Viana Madeira Andre","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":1,"price":15.06,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-10","name":"Viana Madeira Andre","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":1,"price":15.02,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-07","name":"de Souza Funo Elaine Maria","title":"officer: Accounting Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":406,"price":15.25,"total_val":0.01},{"date":"2026-07-13","name":"Viana Madeira Andre","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":9,"price":16,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-06-18","name